out.push(A('**a** Open. ⚠ **Time every reading with a watch and write the ten times up.** **Eighty words takes about thirty seconds.** **Three or four of the ten will run over forty**, which means the words are longer than the facts in them — and the room should be told that interpretation only after all ten times are on the board.'));
out.push(A('**b** Would survive: **3** and **4**. ⚠ **3 is a count, a denominator and a named document; 4 is a shared figure and a disagreement in one sentence, which is 8.5.** **1 has _claimed_ and _significant_ in nine words; 2 has _it should be noted that_, _a number of_ and an idiom; 5 has _clearly_ and _major_ and no fact at all.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 2 · Listen and read'));
out.push(A('**a** **B** — **the whole of this unit applied at once, under a clock**: the free verb, no changeable word, the strike test passed, and nothing in it a stranger would have to decide about.'));
out.push(A('**b** **1** ⚠ **About five minutes writing and thirty-five on the telephone**, because the eighty words are made of counts and denominators and dates and he does not have them when the story starts.   **2** **She reads them twice and sends them** — **and the second read is for sense rather than for faults, which happens about once a week.**'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **The draft at minute five is a shape with holes in it, and this is the instruction the class will not follow unless it is made mechanical.** **Make them write the shape with blanks, on paper, before any finished sentence exists** — _"___ of the eleven districts in ___ have no fixed clinic, according to ___."_ **Then count the blanks and name the calls.** **A student who drafts sentences first will spend the time making the prose good and produce eighty words with no figures in them**, and no desk and no reader can put figures into a document. ⚠ **The time split is the finding, not the word count**: five, thirty-five, three. **Give it as three numbers and let the room do the subtraction.**'));
out.push(S('Language box · Practise'));
out.push(A('**1** **The new thing with its number, in the first twenty words.**   **2** **The thing it is in dispute with, in the same sentence where possible** — **which is 8.5.**   **3** **The fourth paragraph, written knowing it will be cut.**   **4** ⚠ **The eighty words of something you have already written at length** — **and in this class a third of those have turned out to be unwritable.**   **5** ⚠ **Where they cannot be written, the finding is that the document has nothing in it yet**, and that is worth forty minutes rather than four months.'));
out.push(S('Stage 3 · Practise (sample – Card A)'));
