out.push(A('**1** _…the pharmacy had instructed **it**…_ ⚠ **Delete _to_.**   **2** _It should be noted that, in a not insignificant number **of** cases…_ **and the whole clause should then go.**   **3** _Non-attendance on three consecutive days **triggers** a letter._   **4** _…to all **intents** and purposes…_   **5** _…what fact has gone with **it**._   **6** _**Said** is the only one of the five **that** takes no position._'));
out.push(S('Stage 2 · Listen and read'));
out.push(A('**b** ⚠ **The two changes are different kinds of thing and must be sorted before either is answered.** **_Recommended_ to _instructed_ is an error of fact and is the desk\'s to correct.** **_Said_ to _claimed_ is a position the desk was entitled to take.** **What follows is one letter and one conversation, in that order**: the letter asks for the correction of fact and says nothing about the verb, because a correction asked for alongside a complaint arrives as part of the complaint.'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **This is the seventh mediation and the first in which half the complaint is not the other party\'s fault at all.** **Sort first and answer second.** **An error of fact is corrected; a position the editor was entitled to is not an error** — **and a letter that asks for both will get neither.** ⚠ **Then the half of the finding that belongs to the writer, and it must not be skipped because it is uncomfortable**: the edit landed where it did because there was nothing else in the sentence to land on. **No date, no decider, no document.** **A desk does not invent a doubt: it finds the one place a doubt will fit.** **Say the first half in a letter and the second half to yourself** — **and the second is the half that stops it happening again.**'));
out.push(NOTE('**The four-sentence letter is the deliverable and the fourth sentence is where every class fails.** ⚠ **The printed words. The sent words. The document, with its date and who holds it. The correction asked for.** **Then stop.** **Everybody wants to add a clause after _I should be grateful for a correction_** — _as the matter is of some importance_, _as I am sure you will appreciate_ — **and that clause is the whole of what turns a request into an argument.** ⚠ **Mark the letters on this one point before anything else.** **A desk shown its own copy against a dated document does not refuse; it refuses when the letter argues**, because the question then becomes whether the writer is reasonable, and that question has no document behind it.'));
