out.push(SAMPLE(['Mrs Ajouz has two complaints and they feel like one, which is the problem: recommended to instructed is a fact and it is wrong, and said to claimed is about her. Mrs Khoury said only the first is hers to correct, because the second is a position the desk is entitled to take — and if both go in one letter, the correction of the first will arrive as part of a complaint about the second. Mrs Tarabishi asked whether that means two letters, and one letter and one conversation, in that order: the letter asks for the correction of fact and says nothing about the verb, and the conversation about the verb happens after the correction has run, because a desk that has just corrected itself will listen to anything. Mr Shihabi said the verb conversation goes nowhere, and Mrs Khoury said it goes somewhere it is not expected to: the answer will be that claimed was used because the sentence had nothing in it — no date, no decider, no document — and a desk looking for the one changeable thing found two. Dr Qabbani said that is a criticism of her sentence and not of the desk, and Mrs Oueidat said it is a description of both, and the mediation has to carry both without choosing: the error of fact is the desk\'s and the exposure to the edit is the writer\'s. Mr Tayara asked what the letter actually says, and four sentences: the printed words, the sent words, the document that settles it, and the correction asked for, with no adjective anywhere in it. Mrs Rizk asked what happens if the desk refuses, and a desk shown its own copy against a dated document does not refuse; it refuses when the letter argues, because then the question becomes whether the writer is reasonable. Mr Attar asked why not ask for both corrections, and Mrs Oueidat said because one of them is not a correction: a desk asked to correct a verb it was entitled to use will defend the verb, and in defending it will find the missing date and the missing decider. Mr Zahreddine said an insurer does this to his opinions and he has stopped minding, and Mrs Khoury said he has stopped minding because nothing in his opinions is changeable. And Mrs Ajouz said the thing she will take away is that one of her two complaints was about her own sentence: she sent a recommendation with no date and no decider in it, and the desk did not invent a doubt but found the one place in nine words where a doubt would fit.']));
